course: dictionary
lesson: 11504
title: Agreed: same opinion, yes, or chosen together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Agreed is the past form of agree, and it has several meanings. In «We agreed to meet at the park at three», agreed means you and your friend both said yes to the same plan. Ask yourself: did people decide something together?
explain: «Mia and Sam agreed that the blue team had won.» Here agreed means they had the same opinion. Agreed can also be an adjective: «The agreed time is four o'clock» means the time everyone chose together. When someone says «Agreed!» on its own, they mean "Yes, I accept."
explain: Context tells you which meaning it is. Swap in "said yes to", "had the same opinion" or "decided together" and see which one still makes sense. Phrases like agreed with, agreed to, agreed on and as agreed often show the meaning too.
fact: Agree is the base word, and agreed is its past form.
fact: «Agreed» can mean had the same opinion as someone.
fact: «Agreed» can mean said yes to something, like a plan.
fact: «Agreed» as an adjective means decided by everyone together, like «an agreed time».
fact: Phrases: agreed with, agreed to, agreed on, as agreed, it was agreed that.
exercise: «We agreed to meet at the park at three.» What does agreed mean here? | Ran all the way home | Forgot all about the plan | *Said yes to the plan | Had a loud argument
exercise: «Ella and Jo agreed that the blue team had won.» What does agreed mean? | *Had the same opinion as each other | Shouted at each other | Lost their bags | Gave up on the game
exercise: In «The agreed time was ten o'clock», what does agreed mean? | Forgotten | *Decided by everyone together | Broken | Very loud
test: «Mr Patel and the class agreed on the rules before the game started.» What does agreed mean? | Argued loudly | Ran off | *Decided together by everyone | Lost the rules
test: Ben suggests pizza. Ana says «Agreed!» What does she mean? | No way | Maybe later | *Yes, I accept | I am tired
exam: «Tom wanted to play football, but Ana wanted to read, and they agreed to go to the library.» What does agreed to mean here? | Forgot about the library | Argued until the library closed | Sat down to rest | *Said yes to going to the library
